      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The clinical findings in 56 patients with hepatic amebiasis are reviewed. This illness was most frequent in male black patients, 20-39 years old. The clinical picture is dominated by upper right quadrant abdominal pain, general malaise, pain on percussion of the right hypochondrium and tender hepatomegaly. Jaundice is not rare and appears to have no prognostic significance. The importance of early diagnosis is emphasized."},
